  "title": "Chains of knots off parity laws: they split from bond distance exactly at gates",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Of the 1,156 laws made of two three-place knots sharing one distinction, a knot contains both far ends exactly when the knots do not meet at a gate (a value of the shared distinction satisfying both); then the least such knot has four distinctions, and in the 72 gated laws no knot does. For chains of up to four single clauses, a knot spans the chain exactly when every shared distinction is read with opposite signs by its two clauses. The NAND thread's only knots are its clauses.",
